==English==
{{was wotd|2011|December|12}}

===Etymology===
{{calque|en|la|advocātus diabolī||the devil’s advocate}}, a popular title given to the officer dealing with the [[canonization]] process in the 16th c.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-au-devil's advocate.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[devil]]'s [[advocate]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} One who [[debate]]s from a viewpoint which he or she may not actually hold, usually to determine its [[validity]] or simply for the sake of [[argument]].
# {{lb|en|Roman Catholic}} A [[canon]] lawyer appointed by the [[Church]] to argue against the [[canonization]] of the proposed [[candidate]].

